But some nights, lying awake, I feel it still:
the slow pull backward, the long hesitation,
the water deciding, again, to come home.','The final lines of the poem most strongly suggest that the speaker',NULL,'["regrets ever having lived near the marsh","prefers the predictable rivers of her new home","has forgotten the lessons her grandmother taught her","still feels drawn back toward the place where she grew up"]',3,'The "slow pull backward" and the water "deciding, again, to come home" link the tide''s reversal to the speaker''s lingering pull toward home.',1,0);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (id,exam_type,section,kind,difficulty,passage,stem,image_svg,choices,answer,explanation,active,created_at) VALUES ('seed-map-reading-7e698df8bc89','MAP','reading','mcq',4,'With four hundred meters left, Dev was in fifth place, and fifth place did not qualify for anything.

He had run this race in his head a hundred times on the drive up, and in every version he had made his move at the final curve, sweeping past the leaders with a grace he had never actually possessed. Now the curve was coming, and his legs felt like borrowed equipment—heavy, unfamiliar, returned in worse condition than promised.

Ahead of him, the runner from Lakeview glanced over his shoulder. It was a small thing, a half-second turn of the head, but Coach Ferris had drilled it into them all season: a runner who looks back is a runner who is worried. Dev felt something shift in his chest, a door unlatching.

He did not sweep past anyone. He clawed. He passed the Lakeview runner on the inside with his elbows flailing and his mouth open like a gasping fish, and then he passed another, and then the finish line was simply there, closer than it had any right to be.

Third. He bent over, hands on his knees, and laughed—a cracked, breathless sound that surprised him. It looked nothing like the race in his head. It was better, he decided, because it was real.','The contrast between the race Dev imagined and the race he actually ran mainly develops which theme?',NULL,'["Careful planning is the only reliable path to success.","A real achievement, however awkward, can mean more than an idealized fantasy.","Coaches understand races better than the athletes who run them.","Competition tends to bring out the worst in people."]',1,'Dev concludes that the clumsy, real race "was better... because it was real," valuing genuine effort over his graceful daydream.',1,0);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions (id,exam_type,section,kind,difficulty,passage,stem,image_svg,choices,answer,explanation,active,created_at) VALUES ('seed-map-reading-e507d9f1c2c2','MAP','reading','mcq',4,'With four hundred meters left, Dev was in fifth place, and fifth place did not qualify for anything.

